## 🔄 Orchestrator State Machine Diagram

The orchestrator enforces strict state persistence via `sandbox/dashboards/<dashboard-name>/agent/plan-follower.md`. If interrupted, the agent reads the plan file to resume execution:

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> InitConfig: User initiates request

    state "Step 1: Smart Config Setup" as InitConfig {
        [*] --> ExtractParams
        ExtractParams --> SetDefaults: Infer dashboard-name & store target
        SetDefaults --> CreatePlan: Create plan-follower.md
    }

    InitConfig --> Step2_PromptGen

    state "Step 2: Reverse Prompt Generation" as Step2_PromptGen {
        [*] --> CallReverseSkill
        CallReverseSkill --> WritePromptFile
    }

    Step2_PromptGen --> Step3_BatchCollection: Update plan-follower.md

    state "Step 3: Batch Artifact Collection" as Step3_BatchCollection {
        [*] --> CheckFileSystem
        CheckFileSystem --> AutoAdvance: All 3 files present on disk
        CheckFileSystem --> AwaitSingleGate: Files missing
        AwaitSingleGate --> UserSavesFiles: User saves specifications, CSV, and HTML
        UserSavesFiles --> AutoAdvance: User clicks "Confirm Artifacts Saved"
    }

    Step3_BatchCollection --> Step4_HTMLSplit: Update plan-follower.md

    state "Step 4: HTML & CSS Auto-Split" as Step4_HTMLSplit {
        [*] --> RunSplitScript
        RunSplitScript --> CoLocateAssets: Write styles.css, script.js, and HTML to iframe-html/
    }

    Step4_HTMLSplit --> Step5_DualPassCompilation: Update plan-follower.md

    state "Step 5: Dual-Pass React Compilation" as Step5_DualPassCompilation {
        [*] --> Pass1_Blueprint
        Pass1_Blueprint --> Pass2_CodeGeneration: Automatic progression
        Pass2_CodeGeneration --> EmitCodebase: Write to react-clone/
    }

    Step5_DualPassCompilation --> Step6_BuildVerify: Update plan-follower.md

    state "Step 6: Build Verification & Final Handoff" as Step6_BuildVerify {
        [*] --> ExecNpmBuild
        ExecNpmBuild --> MarkAllCompleted
        MarkAllCompleted --> HandoffSummary
    }

    Step6_BuildVerify --> [*]
```

---

## 📋 Step-by-Step 6-Phase Pipeline

| Step | Action | Execution Type | Primary Output / Artifact |
| :---: | :--- | :---: | :--- |
| **1** | Init & Smart Config Setup | Automated | Sets config defaults & creates `sandbox/dashboards/<dashboard-name>/agent/plan-follower.md` |
| **2** | Generate Reverse Prompt | Automated | Generates `sandbox/dashboards/<dashboard-name>/reverse-prompt-<feature-name>.md` |
| **3** | Batch Artifact Collection | User / Auto-Detected | Collects `specifications.md`, `<dashboard-name>-data.csv`, and `iframe-html/<dashboard-name>.html` |
| **4** | Auto HTML Split | Automated | Splits DOM into `styles.css`, `script.js`, and cleaned HTML inside `iframe-html/` |
| **5** | Dual-Pass React Compilation | Automated | Generates full React codebase inside `sandbox/dashboards/<dashboard-name>/react-clone/` |
| **6** | Build Verification & Handoff | Automated | Runs `npm run build`, marks ledger completed, and presents output paths |

> 💡 **Note on HTML DOM Extraction Procedure** to obtain `iframe.html`:
> 1. Open Google Sheets in Google Chrome and launch Chrome Developer Tools (Inspector).
> 2. Right-click the root iframe element or its inner `<html>` element.
> 3. Select **Edit as HTML**, copy the full content.
> 4. Paste into `sandbox/dashboards/<dashboard-name>/iframe-html/<dashboard-name>.html`.

---

## 📁 Staged Artifact Directory Layout

During execution, all input and output files are cleanly isolated inside the sandbox hierarchy:

```text
sandbox/
└── dashboards/
    └── <dashboard-name>/
        ├── agent/
        │   └── plan-follower.md             # Persistent State Machine Tracking Ledger
        │
        ├── reverse-prompt-<feature-name>.md  # Generated Gemini Canvas reverse prompt
        ├── specifications.md                 # Input 1: Gemini Canvas 7-Tab Spec (SPEC_IR)
        ├── <dashboard-name>-data.csv         # Input 2: Raw CSV Dataset (DATA_IR)
        │
        ├── iframe-html/                      # Co-located HTML split assets (Input 3 DOM_IR)
        │   ├── <dashboard-name>.html         # Cleaned DOM layout (Rendering-Only Mode)
        │   ├── styles.css                    # Extracted Tailwind CSS v4 design tokens
        │   └── script.js                     # Extracted non-React script block
        │
        └── react-clone/                      # Generated standalone React feature codebase
            ├── src/
            │   ├── components/               # Adapted shadcn/ui & feature layout components
            │   ├── features/                 # Main feature modules, stores, and utilities
            │   └── styles/                   # Scoped Tailwind CSS v4 directives
            └── package.json
```

---

## 🚀 How to Start Using This Orchestrator

1. In VS Code, open a new Copilot AI chat session.
2. Select the `@gsheet-to-react-orchestrator` agent.
3. Enter: `@gsheet-to-react-orchestrator Start cloning my dashboard "<GSHEET_DASHBOARD_CANVAS_NAME>"` to start the migration process.

The orchestrator will automatically configure the pipeline, generate the reverse engineering prompt, detect saved input files, and produce a fully built, verified React application.
